                        <h2>We Tested Dirty Frag in Kubernetes: EKS and GKE Were Exploitable When Seccomp Was Unset</h2>
                        <p>We tested Dirty Frag on EKS, GKE, Talos, and kind. EKS and GKE reached container root when seccomp was unset or Unconfined; RuntimeDefault blocked the tested xfrm chain; PSS Restricted blocked the full PoC on GKE and blocked tested prerequisites on EKS and Talos; and Talos blocked Unconfined because user namespaces were disabled.</p>
